      "text": [
        "820 - وَقَالَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «إِنِّي لَأَعْجَبُ مِمَّنْ يَأْخُذُ فِي حَاجَةٍ وَ هُوَ عَلَى وُضُوءٍ كَيْفَ لاَ تُقْضَى حَاجَتُهُ وَ إِنِّي لَأَعْجَبُ مِمَّنْ يَأْخُذُ فِي حَاجَةٍ وَ هُوَ مُعْتَمٌّ تَحْتَ حَنَكِهِ كَيْفَ لاَ تُقْضَى حَاجَتُهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.820 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), said:\n\"I am amazed by one who goes about seeking to fulfil a need while in a state of ritual purity (wudu) — how is it that his need is not met?\nAnd I am amazed by one who seeks to fulfil a need while wearing his turban wrapped under his chin — how is it that his need is not met?\""
        ]
      }
    },
